(Lesson 1: Three Categories of Arabic Words \(Aqsam Al-Kalimah\)) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 12 Tf
13.7999999999999989 TL
0.063 0.176 0.137 rg
54. 731.8899999999999864 Td
(Every meaningful Arabic word falls into one of three categories: Ism \(Noun — names of persons,) Tj
T* (places, concepts, or adjectives\), Fil \(Verb — past Madi, present/future Mudari, and imperative Amr\),) Tj
T* (and Harf \(Particle — prepositions and conjunctions\).) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 12 Tf
13.7999999999999989 TL
0.063 0.176 0.137 rg
54. 666.8899999999999864 Td
(Recognizing word endings \(Irab\) reveals grammatical function: Raf \(nominative, usually Dammah\),) Tj
T* (Nasb \(accusative, usually Fathah\), and Jarr \(genitive, usually Kasrah for nouns\).) Tj
ET
BT
