(Lesson 2: The Nominal Sentence \(Al-Jumlah Al-Ismiyyah\)) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 12 Tf
13.7999999999999989 TL
0.063 0.176 0.137 rg
54. 731.8899999999999864 Td
(A nominal sentence begins with a noun and has two essential parts: Al-Mubtada \(the subject,) Tj
T* (typically definite and nominative\) and Al-Khabar \(the predicate, typically indefinite and nominative,) Tj
T* (agreeing in gender and number\).) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 12 Tf
13.7999999999999989 TL
0.063 0.176 0.137 rg
54. 666.8899999999999864 Td
(Example: Al-Kitabu nafiun \(The book is beneficial\). Al-Madrasatu jamilatun \(The school is) Tj
T* (beautiful\). Prepositions \(Huruf Al-Jarr\) such as fi \(in\), ila \(to\), min \(from\), and ala \(upon\) place the) Tj
T* (following noun into the Majrur \(genitive\) state.) Tj
ET
BT
